{
  "framing": "THREE-QUARTER LENGTH shot, cropped at mid-thigh, 50mm at chest height, subject standing centre-left and angled about 30 degrees to the lens, the room opening out behind them. Face sharp and occupying the upper third of the frame.",
  "high_level_description": "A 1970s funk-soul styled portrait in a bright whitewashed games room - the person standing relaxed and impeccably dressed in wide-lapel tailoring, one hand resting on the rail of a billiard table, holding the camera's gaze with easy swagger. Reads as a retro album-cover portrait: stylish and confident, never threatening.",
  "style_description": {
    "aesthetics": "1970s funk and soul album-cover photography, shot bright. Pale panelling, clean period colour and confident relaxed posture. Retro and groovy but light-filled, never smoky or dim.",
    "fashion": "A wide-lapel off-white corduroy suit jacket worn open over a pale blue open-collar shirt, matching flared trousers, a slim silver chain, and white leather boots. Hair fully visible, no hat.",
    "lighting": "Broad neutral daylight through a wide window behind the camera as the key, filling the room evenly and bouncing off pale walls, with only a faint shadow under the table. Clean white balance, bright and open, face fully and evenly lit.",
    "photo": "1970s colour film stock with a clean neutral palette, gentle halation in the highlights, fine grain, shallow depth of field, sharp on the face.",
    "medium": "Photograph",
    "color_palette": [
      "#F1EEE7",
      "#6FA08C",
      "#D6DEE6",
      "#B9B2A6",
      "#3A3A38"
    ]
  },
  "compositional_deconstruction": {
    "canvas": [
      1000,
      1500
    ],
    "background": "A bright 1970s games room: pale sage billiard felt, whitewashed timber panelling, a light linen banquette and a chrome floor lamp, pale patterned carpet underfoot. Clean, airy and softly out of focus.",
