    "fashion": "A plain black fine-gauge knit, only the neckline entering the frame.",
    "lighting": "Hard directional daylight from one side carving a crisp light-to-shade transition down the face, with a large white bounce close in on the opposite side so the shadow side stays open and fully detailed. Nothing goes black.",
    "photo": "Black-and-white 35mm negative film, visible silver grain, a long open tonal scale, critical focus on the eyes, real pore texture and no retouching.",
